# Build output for all workspace members.
/target

# Probe harness run artifacts: logs, screenshots, pid files. The harness writes
# these next to itself; none of it belongs in history.
crates/orca-probe/run*.log
crates/orca-probe/run*.err
crates/orca-probe/run*.pid
crates/orca-probe/run*.png

# Cargo.lock policy: COMMITTED, on purpose.
#
# `cargo` treats this repo as an *application* workspace (three binaries/libs
# that ship as one program, not a library published to crates.io), and the
# guidance for applications is to commit the lockfile. Committing it pins the
# transitive dependency set, which matters far more than usual here: the GPUI
# dependency is a git pin into Zed's `main`-adjacent history, so an unpinned
# resolve is not reproducible by default.
#
# Do not add `/Cargo.lock` to this file.
